  "contract": [
    "Shim creates a persistent runtime-managed VM record named by sandbox ID before starting the VM.",
    "VM inserts, upsert updates and deletes use the same SQLite vms table; journal triggers share those transactions.",
    "Persisted Linux PID start time is /proc stat field 22 in clock ticks, not wall-clock seconds.",
    "Boot argv is the installed shim executable, _boot-vm and the VM directory boot-config.json path.",
    "The engine pre-creates a per-VM readiness marker in shared rootfs. Doorbell success can leave it empty. Only exact, regular, single-link, zero-byte markers bound to journaled sandbox IDs are runtime bookkeeping.",
    "Node inspection does not call machine status/start/stop/delete. Release manager observation can create a VM directory; the later reference changes that behavior."
  ]
